{"parentUuid":"98a2e7f5-e493-4789-b2bf-38893c093714","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"ac494304c28cb7af7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01D8iTJQQwYAfkq39jHm2L4z","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Belief Propagation CSP placement constraint satisfaction 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Constraint Satisfaction Problems (CSP) in Artificial Intelligence - GeeksforGeeks\",\"url\":\"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/artificial-intelligence/constraint-satisfaction-problems-csp-in-artificial-intelligence/\"},{\"title\":\"CS 294. Constraint Satisfaction Problems, Spring 2025\",\"url\":\"https://people.eecs.berkeley.edu/~prasad/spring2025.html\"},{\"title\":\"Artiﬁcial Intelligence Constraint Satisfaction Problems Marc Toussaint\",\"url\":\"https://www.user.tu-berlin.de/mtoussai/teaching/19-ArtificialIntelligence/08-CSP.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Constraint satisfaction problem - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Constraint_satisfaction_problem\"},{\"title\":\"Constraint satisfaction problems: Algorithms and applications - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0377221798003646\"},{\"title\":\"Solving Constraint Satisfaction Problems through Belief ...\",\"url\":\"https://web.stanford.edu/~montanar/RESEARCH/FILEPAP/all07_ksat.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"CONSTRAINT SATISFACTION PROBLEMS(CSP) | by Kanchanakanta | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@kanchanakanta/constraint-satisfaction-problems-csp-766f3ddeed3f\"},{\"title\":\"31st International Conference on Principles and Practice of Constraint Programming (CP 2025)\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/volume/LIPIcs-volume-340\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) A Belief Propagation Algorithm for Constraint Satisfaction Problem Based on Backtracking\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/369286153_A_Belief_Propagation_Algorithm_for_Constraint_Satisfaction_Problem_Based_on_Backtracking\"},{\"title\":\"A residual-based message passing algorithm for constraint satisfaction problems\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2202.12468\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about Belief Propagation applied to Constraint Satisfaction Problems. Here's what the research shows:\n\n## Belief Propagation for CSPs\n\nMessage passing algorithms capture complicated interactions among interconnected variables in complex systems and extract information from the fixed point of iterated messages, providing a powerful toolkit in tackling hard computational tasks in optimization, inference, and learning problems.\n\n### Recent Research (2025)\n\nBelief propagation (BP) guided decimation algorithms using asynchronous updating strategy are being applied to solve random constraint satisfaction problems with growing domains referred to as model RB. These algorithms improve the convergence of message updating and increase the success probability in finding solutions around the satisfiability threshold with a low computational cost.\n\n### Addressing Hard CSP Instances\n\nWhen a control parameter (such as constraint density) is tuned in CSPs, multiple threshold phenomena emerge, signaling fundamental structural transitions in their solution space. Finding solutions around these transition points is exceedingly challenging for algorithm design, where message passing algorithms suffer from a large message fluctuation far from convergence.\n\n### Recent Algorithmic Improvements\n\nA residual-based updating step has been introduced into message passing algorithms, in which messages varying large between consecutive steps are given high priority in the updating process. For the specific example of model RB, a typical prototype of random CSPs with growing domains, this algorithm improves the convergence of message updating and increases the success probability in finding solutions around the satisfiability threshold.\n\nThe 2025 Constraint Programming Conference (CP 2025) has also been documenting recent advances in CSP solving techniques and their applications.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"7a6e7126-075b-4a08-9718-f63bc6336598","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:52:18.006Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"98a2e7f5-e493-4789-b2bf-38893c093714","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"dbf2e1ec-d2df-4ca5-9d35-e56aa6090347","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"ac494304c28cb7af7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014kXnhu8aZ2rE8Wvc7GfRFy","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Survey Propagation SAT solver 2024 2025 industrial CDCL hybrid\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Massively Parallel Continuous Local Search for Hybrid SAT Solving on GPUs\",\"url\":\"https://ojs.aaai.org/index.php/AAAI/article/view/33211/35366\"},{\"title\":\"Journal of Artificial Intelligence Research 1 (2024) 1-37\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2402.10705\"},{\"title\":\"Unlocking Optimization: A Manager's Guide to SAT-Based Techniques | Empowering Enterprises with Data-Driven Solutions\",\"url\":\"https://www.logicclutch.com/blog/sat-based-optimization-managers-guide\"},{\"title\":\"Automatically discovering heuristics in a complex SAT ...\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2507.22876\"},{\"title\":\"Journal of Artificial Intelligence Research 81 (2024) 989-1017\",\"url\":\"https://www.jair.org/index.php/jair/article/download/16163/27111/42883\"},{\"title\":\"CDCL SAT Solver Heuristics: Clause Management, Instance Structure, and\",\"url\":\"https://summit.sfu.ca/_flysystem/fedora/2025-07/etd21616.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"SAT solver - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SAT_solver\"},{\"title\":\"Enhancing Modern SAT Solver With Machine Learning Method | Proceedings of the Great Lakes Symposium on VLSI 2025\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3716368.3735251\"},{\"title\":\"On the Structure of the Boolean Satisfiability Problem: A Survey\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/366788583_On_the_Structure_of_the_Boolean_Satisfiability_Problem_A_Survey\"},{\"title\":\"SAT-Solving: Performance Analysis of Survey Propagation and DPLL\",\"url\":\"https://q4.github.io/satcmp.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, here's what I found regarding survey propagation, SAT solvers, and hybrid approaches in recent research:\n\n## Survey Propagation and SAT Solving\n\nSurvey propagation (SP) is often used for random SAT instances and involves passing \"messages\" between clauses and variables to guide the search. However, the search results indicate that survey propagation is not the dominant approach in modern industrial SAT solving.\n\n## CDCL as the Industrial Standard\n\nMost state-of-the-art SAT solvers are based on the CDCL framework as of 2019. Almost all modern SAT solvers working on industrial formulas use the CDCL algorithm. This dominance continues in recent work, with CDCL solvers being commonly applied in SOTA hybrid SAT solvers.\n\n## Hybrid Approaches (2024-2025)\n\nRecent research has explored hybrid SAT solving methods combining different techniques:\n\n- The integration of CDCL and Continuous Local Search (CLS) results in FastFourierMaxSAT. However, given industrial problems, FastFourier(Max)SAT might not be competitive with mature CDCL solvers submitted to the competitions.\n\n- Recent advances have explored the integration of neural networks (NN), particularly graph neural networks (GNNs), to improve the performance of existing SAT solvers.\n\n- Joint experiments with the state-of-the-art CDCL solver Kissat systematically evaluate two application paradigms: a hard-constraint strategy that aggressively fixes high-confidence variables to reduce the search space, and a soft-constraint guidance strategy that preserves solver completeness while achieving consistent speedups.\n\nThe results suggest that while various hybrid approaches combining CDCL with machine learning, local search, and other techniques are being explored in 2024-2025, CDCL-based solvers remain the dominant approach for industrial SAT solving problems.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"a8f6add9-241b-4739-90b0-b4e21bb13ad2","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:52:18.053Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"dbf2e1ec-d2df-4ca5-9d35-e56aa6090347","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"00fd7a99-0410-41df-ba3c-891adb5d74ea","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"ac494304c28cb7af7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RY9gy1BMWuuFevGyFX9v8Y","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"GNN belief propagation SAT solver neural message passing 2024 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Neural Approaches to SAT Solving: Design Choices and Interpretability\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2504.01173\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding GNNs for Boolean Satisfiability through Approximation Algorithms\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2408.15418v1\"},{\"title\":\"SAT-GATv2: A Dynamic Attention-Based Graph Neural Network for Solving Boolean Satisfiability Problem\",\"url\":\"https://www.mdpi.com/2079-9292/14/3/423\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Fast Deep Belief Propagation: An Efficient Learning-Based Algorithm for Solving Constraint Optimization Problems\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/396766940_Fast_Deep_Belief_Propagation_An_Efficient_Learning-Based_Algorithm_for_Solving_Constraint_Optimization_Problems\"},{\"title\":\"Fast Deep Belief Propagation: An Efficient Learning-Based Algorithm for Solving Constraint Optimization Problems\",\"url\":\"https://www.mdpi.com/2227-7390/13/20/3349\"},{\"title\":\"Belief Propagation Neural Networks\",\"url\":\"https://proceedings.neurips.cc/paper_files/paper/2020/file/07217414eb3fbe24d4e5b6cafb91ca18-Paper.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"NSNet: A General Neural Probabilistic Framework for Satisfiability Problems\",\"url\":\"https://proceedings.neurips.cc/paper_files/paper/2022/file/a40462acc6959034c6aa6dfb8e696415-Paper-Conference.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Theory-guided Message Passing Neural Network for Probabilistic Inference\",\"url\":\"https://proceedings.mlr.press/v238/cui24a/cui24a.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Enhancing Modern SAT Solver With Machine Learning Method | Proceedings of the Great Lakes Symposium on VLSI 2025\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3716368.3735251\"},{\"title\":\"[2507.01825] MILP-SAT-GNN: Yet Another Neural SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.01825\"}]\n\nI've performed the web search for your query. Here are the key findings related to GNN, belief propagation, SAT solvers, and neural message passing from 2024-2025:\n\n## Recent Research Highlights\n\n**Theoretical Connections:**\nThe message passing (MP) process of a GNN can be interpreted through the lens of Belief Propagation algorithms, which operate on similar literal-clause factor graphs. Recent research demonstrates that message-passing GNNs can implement gradient-based optimization of SDP relaxations.\n\n**Novel GNN-Based SAT Solvers (2024-2025):**\n\n1. SAT-GATv2 is a GNN-based model designed to solve Boolean satisfiability through graph-based deep learning, transforming SAT formulas into graph structures and leveraging message-passing neural networks (MPNNs) to propagate information (January 2025).\n\n2. NSNet is a GNN framework that extends belief propagation in the latent space, and can be considered a neural version of BP that generalizes it in the vector space with learnable parameters.\n\n**Deep Belief Propagation Approaches (2025):**\nFast Deep Belief Propagation (FDBP) is a deep learning framework that improves COP solving through online self-supervised learning and GPU acceleration, improving memory usage and scalability of deep belief propagation (October 2025).\n\n**Integration with Classical Solvers:**\nRecent work presents GNN-based algorithms that predict backbone variables for SAT instances and UNSAT-core variables using Weighted Literal-Incidence Graphs encoded with GNNs (2025).\n\n**Latest Developments (July 2025):**\nMILP-SAT-GNN enables GNNs to solve SAT problems by leveraging techniques developed for applying GNNs to Mixed Integer Linear Programming.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"0e9b5fce-452c-4da4-ba8e-c0134a8673a3","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:52:20.152Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"00fd7a99-0410-41df-ba3c-891adb5d74ea","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
