{"parentUuid":"e638f410-dc47-4fc8-b1cb-9fc773170ce2","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"ac494304c28cb7af7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015U4VYPyyTwoq7jNF8zCNoY","type":"tool_result","content":"I appreciate your question, but I need to be transparent: the content you've provided appears to be a PDF file encoded in binary format (compressed/flattened streams), which I cannot meaningfully parse or extract information from.\n\nTo answer your questions about NSNet properly, I would need:\n- Plain text documentation or research papers about NSNet\n- Information about its relationship to backpropagation (BP)\n- Details on training data requirements\n- Documentation on its use as hints for SAT solvers\n- Assessment of industrial applicability\n\n**What I can tell you:** NSNet typically refers to neural network approaches for constraint satisfaction or symbolic reasoning tasks. However, without accessing the actual document content, I cannot provide the specific details you're requesting about:\n\n1. NSNet's architecture and BP relationship\n2. Training data specifications\n3. SAT solver integration capabilities\n4. Production-readiness assessment\n\nCould you provide the information in one of these formats instead?\n- Plain text summary\n- Markdown document\n- Link to a research paper\n- Direct text excerpts\n\nThis would allow me to give you an accurate, detailed response addressing each of your four specific questions.\n\n[Binary content (application/pdf, 459.7KB) also saved to C:\\Users\\22957\\.claude\\projects\\D--claude-pj-zmd\\7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9\\tool-results\\webfetch-1778190772899-sz8fwc.pdf]"}]},"uuid":"92b90819-fcfd-4941-bc92-81ccc50011a9","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:52:57.243Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e638f410-dc47-4fc8-b1cb-9fc773170ce2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-